content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-201 — Velatek VX-90 dosing pump, serial VX-5531",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Reported reading: chemical leakage at the diaphragm/head of about 2 drops per second. Applicable limit: no Velatek VX-90 external-leakage or diaphragm-leak limit is supplied, so a documented numeric pass/fail comparison cannot be made. The AquaDyne HF-300 bearing-temperature limits (normal up to 70 C, alarm 80 C, trip 90 C) and HF-300 vibration limits (Zone D 7.1–11.0 mm/s RMS, labelled 'stop the pump') concern different parameters and a different pump; neither applies to this leak.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reported motor condition: 'running normally', which is qualitative rather than a measured reading. Applicable limit: no VX-90 motor condition limit or motor measurement is supplied. The HF-300 figures of 1480 rpm, 55 kW and 400 V are equipment ratings for another asset, not acceptance limits that can verify P-201's motor condition.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Take P-201 out of service for the active chemical leak and keep it isolated pending an asset-specific repair plan. This immediate-stop decision is a precautionary planner decision, not a claimed VX-90 documented leak-limit trip; all intrusive work must follow SSP-07.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before opening the pump head or working inside the pump, electrically isolate and apply lock-out/tag-out at the MCC.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves. Drain and vent first, and comply with the line-break permit requirement before breaking into the pump head or associated line.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use chemical goggles and nitrile gloves for the chemical-exposure/line-opening work. Do not identify the chemical as sodium hypochlorite from the supplied evidence: that duty is expressly described only for P-101 to P-106, not P-201.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not disassemble P-201 using the supplied mechanical-seal procedure: it is the AquaDyne HF-300 back-pull-out/impeller/seal procedure, not a Velatek VX-90 diaphragm procedure. Hold diaphragm removal and replacement until the correct VX-90 instructions and parts are available.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not apply the supplied torques of 210 Nm (M16 casing bolts), 160 Nm (M24 impeller nut), 25 Nm (M10 seal gland nuts) or 85 Nm (M12 bearing-housing bolts); they are HF-300 values. Add VX-90 head-fastener torques, diaphragm installation steps and post-repair leak-test acceptance criteria only after the applicable Velatek document is obtained.",
      "citations": [
        "C11"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC are mandatory before work inside the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanically isolate both suction and discharge valves before intrusive work.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use the line-break permit process and drain and vent before opening the pump or line.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves for the chemical-line work; confirm the actual chemical and any additional SDS-required protection before starting.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Applicability decision: the equipment manual evidence is for an AquaDyne HF-300, whereas the faulty asset is a Velatek VX-90, serial VX-5531. No serial range, date or other evidence links VX-5531 to that manual. Consequently, its seal-leak troubleshooting, seal-replacement procedure, torque table, standard labour times, temperature/vibration limits and 68 kg lifting information must not be used as VX-90 maintenance requirements.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Applicability decision: SSP-07 Rev 3 states that it covers all pumps on site, so its isolation, line-break and applicable PPE controls provide the safety basis for this work order. C16 is narrower and identifies sodium-hypochlorite dosing only on P-101 to P-106; it does not establish P-201's chemical service. There is no direct disagreement between two VX-90 technical documents because none is supplied.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Which Velatek VX-90 manual revision applies to serial VX-5531? No Velatek serial ranges, document dates or revision-applicability data are provided.",
    "What is the manufacturer/site allowable external-leakage limit and run-versus-stop criterion for a VX-90 diaphragm/head leak of about 2 drops per second? The immediate stop here is precautionary, not based on a supplied numeric leak threshold.",
    "What is the root cause of the reported diaphragm/head leak? The evidence does not support assigning the HF-300 mechanical-seal causes (worn/cracked seal faces, dry running or shaft misalignment) to this different pump and leak location.",
    "What are the correct diaphragm, head seal/gasket and any other required part numbers and quantities? No VX-90 parts information is supplied, so no parts have been guessed.",
    "What are the VX-90 diaphragm replacement steps, head-fastener sizes and torques, inspection criteria, and post-repair leak-test/return-to-service acceptance criteria?",
    "What labour duration and technician count apply? The supplied 4.0 hours/two technicians for mechanical-seal replacement and other standard times are HF-300 values and have not been transferred to P-201.",
    "What chemical, concentration and SDS apply at P-201, and are respiratory protection, a face shield, protective clothing, emergency shower/eyewash or spill controls required in addition to goggles and nitrile gloves?",
    "Confirm the P-201 MCC isolation point, suction/discharge isolation valves, drain/vent arrangements and safe disposition of drained chemical before issuing the job for execution.",
    "Confirm whether any component lift will exceed 25 kg; if so, SSP-07 requires a supervisor-signed lifting plan and certified lifting equipment. The HF-300's 68 kg back-pull-out mass does not establish a VX-90 lifting requirement.",
    "Confirm the site priority matrix. P1 is a conservative planning assignment for an ongoing chemical release requiring immediate isolation, not an application of the bearing-temperature-above-alarm priority-1 rule, for which P-201 has no applicable reading."
  ]
}
